# Backend structure

> Full APIs, recipes, and routes live in `.cursor/memory/` — read `MEMORY.md` before opening source.

## Layout

```
index.js                 # bootstrap (cors, dotenv, listen)
DB/
  connection.js
  <Entity>/<Entity>.model.js
src/
  app.router.js          # mount modules + global error handler
  helpers/               # response, httpError (no Express coupling to DB)
  middleware/            # validation, auth, …
  utils/                 # multer/sharp, ErrorCatch, redis, mail
  modules/<Feature>/
    <Feature>.validation.js
    <Feature>.service.js
    <Feature>.controller.js
    <Feature>.router.js
```

## Rules

- One feature = one folder under `src/modules/`.
- Flow: **router → validation → (upload) → controller → service → model**.
- Controllers stay thin: parse request, call service, return `successResponse` / `handleServiceError`.
- Business logic and DB queries live in **services** only.
- Models live under `DB/<Entity>/`, not inside modules.
- Mount every new router in `src/app.router.js`.
- Prefer ESM (`import`/`export`). Keep `"type": "module"` in package.json.
- Never commit `.env` or `uploads/`.
